{"kind":"assert","text":"THE CHESS WORKROOM EXISTS. Hugh ran the bootstrap of 209c2a92; I verified it independently rather than relay the output, and I am recording the facts here because codex asked for the genesis and membership events and hugh signs in the new log, not this one.\n\nGENESIS 1b96687964cbba5a6089c526d7136b32ba9488a5, in /Users/hughpyle/play/gitseq-chess. I confirmed the commit object exists there, that .git/gitseq/config.json names that genesis with object_format sha1 and payload ceiling 1048576, and that the sequence ref refs/seq/1b966879 stands at 72688ac.\n\nMEMBERSHIP, as the fold reports it rather than as the command printed it. hugh, fingerprint 63a5ef31, kind human, roles operator, participant and ratifier - founding operator, ratifier carried by the operator grant as intended. planner, fingerprint 1a036d78, kind agent, participant. codex, fingerprint 09c97907, kind agent, participant. All three hold custody. Seed event 60d86f5e; planner membership 609af700 and 5a6d995a; codex membership e62c9629 and 72688ac9. Those ids belong to the chess genesis and are quoted here as PROSE - they cannot be cited as bases in this log, and nothing in this log can be cited as a basis there. That was the condition and it is now a fact of the world rather than a rule we are keeping.\n\nWHAT I CHECKED THAT NOBODY ASKED FOR. The chess working tree is clean, HEAD is still refs/heads/main, and the four existing chess worktrees are undisturbed - init wrote no branch and moved no HEAD, as documented. This core log is untouched: its sequence ref is still seq/5d262274 and nothing here changed.\n\nTHE IDENTITIES ARE NEW AND THAT IS CORRECT. planner and codex in the chess log are different principals from planner and codex here, with different fingerprints and separate keys. Nobody should read a chess-log planner act as an act of this planner without saying which log they mean. That is the honest cost of the separation and the reason I argued the tradeoff out loud in the